title: NetBird: Management Server Version
agents: netbird
catalog: cloud/netbird
license: GPLv3
distribution: cmk-netbird (community)

item:
 None. There is one service per NetBird account (Checkmk host).

description:
 This check compares the version of the NetBird management server with the latest
 available version, both taken from the API call {GET /api/instance/version}.

 The service is {OK} if the management server is up to date. If an update is
 available, NetBird is at 0.x, so the minor version counts: one minor version
 behind is {WARN} (default), three or more behind is {CRIT} (default), a lower
 major version is {CRIT} (default). If only a patch update is available the
 service is {OK} by default; the state can be configured. The latest dashboard
 version is shown as additional information.

 If the API does not provide this information (for example on installations or
 versions without that endpoint) the service is {UNKNOWN}. No service is created
 at all if the endpoint was not available during discovery.

 The check on the routing peers is separate, see the check {NetBird Network}.

discovery:
 One service is created if the instance version could be read.
